### `validate_bfs.py` Error

```
PlotfileError: Data size mismatch in plt02057/Level_0/Cell_D_00000:
expected 18816 doubles, got 16128
```

Root cause: `amrex_reader.py]0;🐋 CodeWhale` line 156 reshapes FAB data as `(ncomp, ny, nx, order='F')` but the correct Fortran-order layout is `(nx, ny, ncomp, order='F')`. The FAB binary contains no separate min/max arrays]0;🐳 CodeWhale — the ASCII header ends and cell data begins immediately. This bug is latent for single-box plotfiles but surfaces with multi-box files (the]0;🐋 CodeWhale BFS case uses two FAB boxes stitched at `x=56`).

