### Notes

- Reattachment at 5.39H is inside the 5–8H literature range and within the ±15% tolerance of Driver & Seegmiller's 6.26.
- The simulation used]0;🐋 CodeWhale 2,057 steps (not 5,000) because `stop_time=0.5` was reached first — the CFL~0.3 on 104×28 grid gives ~20 µs timesteps, so ~]0;🐳 CodeWhale25,000 steps would be needed for 5,000 steps. This is expected behavior.
- `validate_bfs.py` also has a secondary unit bug (`U_REF=44.2` labeled as m/s but]0;🐋 CodeWhale actually ft/s), which would scale Cf/Cp values by ~0.09× but doesn't affect the reattachment detection (sign-based).
